ch.len() == 1 && batch_memory > memory_limit_bytes {\n            // Use non-batch kernel for single oversized trace\n            evaluate_mle_constraints_gpu(...)\n        } else {\n            // Use batch kernel\n            let builder = ZerocheckMleBatchBuilder::new(batch, pk, num_x)?;\n            let out = builder.evaluate(lambda_pows, num_x)?;\n        }\n        batch_start += batch_count;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Result:** Multiple batches can be processed per round, each with independent kernel launch.\n\n---\n\n### 7. CUDA KERNELS INVOKED IN MLE ROUNDS\n\n| Kernel | Type | Location (FFI) | Traces per launch | Notes |\n|--------|------|----------------|-------------------|-------|\n| `zerocheck_batch_eval_mle` | DAG | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs:449` | Multiple | Batch blocks across traces, uses DAG evaluation |\n| `logup_batch_eval_mle` | DAG | Line 463 | Multiple | Batch blocks across traces, DAG for interactions |\n| `zerocheck_monomial_batched` | Monomial | Line 475 | Multiple | Blocks: `ceil(monomials/tpb) * num_y` per trace |\n| `zerocheck_monomial_par_y_batched` | Monomial | Line 487 | Multiple | Optimized for high num_y, auto-tuned chunk size |\n| `logup_monomial_batched` | Monomial | Line 526 | Multiple | Separate contexts for numer/denom monomials |\n| `batched_interpolate_columns` | Utils | Line 251 | Multiple | Descriptor-driven interpolation for all traces |\n\n---\n\n### 8. WHAT WOULD NEED TO CHANGE FOR MULTI-STREAM THREADING\n\nTo implement multi-stream parallelization across threads for the MLE rounds:\n\n#### 1. **Stream Management** \n   - Allocate multiple CUDA streams (e.g., one per OS thread)\n   - Assign each trace batch to a stream\n   - Track stream context in TraceCtx or batch builders\n\n#### 2. **Barrier Before Kernels**\n   - Current code has implicit barrier at D2H (`.to_host()`)\n   - For true async: wrap kernel launch & D2H in thread-local stream tasks\n   - Synchronize all streams at end of `sumcheck_polys_batch_eval`\n\n#### 3. **Memory Management Changes**\n   - VPMM memory pool already supports async frees\n   - Current: cudaFreeAsync ordered by default stream\n   - Multi-stream: ensure device buffer lifetimes outlast kernel execution on assigned stream\n\n#### 4. **Output Accumulation**\n   - Current: sequential D2H, then CPU scatter into `zc_out[trace_idx]`\n   - Multi-stream: collect future handles from thread tasks, synchronize before final gather\n\n#### 5. **Batch Construction Parallelization**\n   - Lines 1292-1308: descriptor building happens on CPU sequentially\n   - Could be parallelized per-batch if descriptor generation is bottleneck\n\n#### 6. **Kernel Launch Ordering**\n   - Current DAG: interpolation → late logup → late zc → early logup → early zc_dag → early zc_mono_high → early zc_mono_low\n   - With streams: late logup/zc could run concurrently, early logup independent of early zc\n\n#### 7. **Memory Limit Accounting**\n   - Current: single `memory_limit_bytes` budget for entire round\n   - Multi-stream: would need per-thread budgets or atomic counter to track peak concurrent usage\n\n---\n\n### 9. KEY FILE PATHS & LINE RANGES\n\n| Component | File | Lines | Purpose |\n|-----------|------|-------|---------|\n| Main loop | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` | 516-533 | Sumcheck round loop invoking `sumcheck_polys_batch_eval` |\n| Per-round evaluation | Same | 1131-1517 | Core per-round MLE orchestration |\n| TraceCtx definition | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle.rs` | 89-105 | Per-trace GPU context |\n| Zerocheck batch builder | Same | 113-254 | DAG-based batch construction & launch |\n| Logup batch builder | Same | 259-408 | Interaction batch construction & launch |\n| Memory-aware batching (zc) | Same | 414-502 | Bin-packing traces across memory limit |\n| Memory-aware batching (logup) | Same | 505-626 | Bin-packing logup traces |\n| Zerocheck monomial batch | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs` | 111-267 | Standard monomial kernel batch |\n| Zerocheck monomial par-Y batch | Same | 281-493 | High num_y optimized monomial batch |\n| Logup monomial batch | Same | 588-793 | Interaction monomial kernel batch |\n| CUDA FFI wrappers | `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` | 449-538 | Kernel function declarations & safe Rust wrappers |\n\n---\n\n### 10. SUMMARY OF PARALLELIZABILITY\n\n**Within a single MLE round round:**\n\n- **Phases 3a-3f are sequential but could be concurrent** (separate streams)\n  - Late logup (3a) and late zc (3b): independent traces, separate output buffers\n  - Early logup (3c) and early zc (3d-3f): independent traces, separate output buffers\n  - Within each path: multiple batches possible, each independent\n\n- **D2H copies block:** `.to_host()` synchronizes current stream\n  - Could use stream-ordered D2H to async-fetch while next kernel prepares\n\n- **CPU scatter operations:** sequential but trivial CPU time\n\n**Bottleneck:** Batched kernel launches on single stream, but multiple batches could run concurrently with proper stream assignment.\n\n**Recommendation for multi-stream:** \n- Assign trace batches to different streams before interpolation phase\n- Keep interpolation on main stream (dependency for all traces)\n- Launch MLE kernels for independent batches on their respective streams\n- Synchronize all streams before CPU reduction phase"}],"totalDurationMs":80204,"totalTokens":91199,"totalToolUseCount":14,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":506,"cache_read_input_tokens":83405,"output_tokens":7284,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":506},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":7284,"cache_read_input_tokens"