{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UKTVSDjMKCAzf5tMBCUxZy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MjNoQXBNwV4ytLYbNDkozL","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-2035-gkr-input-round-robin\n\nReplace contiguous work chunking in GKR input evaluation with interleaved (round-robin) assignment across multi-stream threads. Currently, work items are sorted by descending trace height and split into contiguous chunks via `work_items.chunks(chunk_size)`, causing thread 0 to receive all large AIRs and thread 7 to receive only tiny AIRs. This is the same load imbalance pattern that the Round 0 round-robin optimization fixed (saving 36ms / 1.13x at APC 300). With round-robin assignment, each thread gets a balanced mix of large and small AIRs, reducing the critical thread's wall time and enabling better GPU-stream overlap. At APC 300, GKR input eval is 318ms total (seg0=256ms, seg1=62ms); improved load balance should save 10-25ms.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1000,"cache_read_input_tokens":161772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1000},"output_tokens":41,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8752a685-980c-4a43-bd75-41a76d7996d5","uuid":"1dc99a71-6d69-4612-a3da-778090ebda4b"}
