{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XYnh9FMhZjdnbewPLHkY4b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-13-2035-gkr-input-round-robin\n2\t\n3\tReplace contiguous work chunking in GKR input evaluation with interleaved (round-robin) assignment across multi-stream threads. Currently, work items are sorted by descending trace height and split into contiguous chunks via `work_items.chunks(chunk_size)`, causing thread 0 to receive all large AIRs and thread 7 to receive only tiny AIRs. This is the same load imbalance pattern that the Round 0 round-robin optimization fixed (saving 36ms / 1.13x at APC 300). With round-robin assignment, each thread gets a balanced mix of large and small AIRs, reducing the critical thread's wall time and enabling better GPU-stream overlap. At APC 300, GKR input eval is 318ms total (seg0=256ms, seg1=62ms); improved load balance should save 10-25ms.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FZwBUM4d87p6paUYcN2rEu","session_id":"8752a685-980c-4a43-bd75-41a76d7996d5","uuid":"a2b80811-5b9f-4b98-839c-5ab9821f1782","timestamp":"2026-04-13T18:52:16.871Z"}
